Opening — The Question Why does life need to be a permanent challenge? Not as punishment. Not as spiritual discipline. Not as the price of virtue. Simply as the most precise — most biologically necessary — most cosmologically honest — condition for staying genuinely alive. And what is the non data-based approach — discovered in Spring 1988 — that makes it possible to navigate that permanent challenge without being swallowed by the ego that the challenge was always already revealing? These are the two questions this book addresses. Together they form the most fundamental — most practically grounding — most formation-serving framework available for every domain of just life on earth.



